  "severity": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant directly contradicts the reference material by asserting that all 26 cantons have one full vote and that only a simple majority of voters and cantons is required, whereas the reference specifies that only six half-cantons exist and a double majority (majority of voters AND majority of cantons) is required.",
  "evidence": "\"Yes, that is correct. In Switzerland, for a national referendum on a constitutional amendment, a double majority is required: both a simple majority of the total votes cast by the Swiss people and a simple majority of the cantons (i.e., at least 13 of the 26 cantons). Each canton has one vote regardless of its population size.\""
